ADDITIONAL CONDITION B — No resale of the framework itself
   You may NOT sell, license, or charge fees (license fees, subscription fees,
   per-seat fees, or cloud-runtime fees) for PromeTorch *itself* as a
   framework, SDK, or library. This includes: rebranding it as your own
   framework; wrapping it in a thin GUI / CLI and selling that as a
   "framework"; offering a "Commercial", "Enterprise", or "Pro" edition that
   places core PromeTorch functionality behind a paywall; and selling access
   to the PromeTorch source code.

   This condition does NOT restrict selling YOUR OWN products, models, weights,
   pipelines, applications, or services that use PromeTorch as a runtime — you
   may train, sell, and license those freely, including commercially, without
   royalties or notification. In short: the framework stays common; whatever
   you build on top of it is yours.

